{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792189152,"nonce":"gos+l3R1i2WssvZ645gYUJMAmvY=","title":"CI resolves dependencies fresh, so a yank upstream fails every workflow","message":"From 77183360 on, CI, Documentation, Coverage, Android and iOS Compile all failed at dependency resolution, before compiling anything:\n\n    error: failed to select a version for the requirement `zip = \"^2.2\"`\n      version 2.2.0 is yanked ... version 2.6.1 is yanked\n    required by package `zyntax_compiler` (darmie/zyntax rev 262a7d1e)\n      ... `zyntax_embed` ... `blinc_cn_dsl`\n\n`Cargo.lock` is not tracked, so every run resolves from the crates.io index. zip's maintainers yank all but the newest release of each major; on 2026-10-16 the last 2.x, 2.6.1, was yanked as well, then un-yanked at 17:47 UTC, after the last failing run (17:34). Local builds were unaffected: an existing lockfile may keep a yanked version (it had 2.4.2). zyntax_compiler builds against 2.6.1.\n\nThe failed runs on 00a5ff45 were re-run once 2.6.1 was back.\n\nThe exposure remains: the next yank of 2.6.1 breaks CI the same way. Durable options:\n- zyntax: move `zip` (crates/compiler and crates/zyntax_cli, both `\"2.2\"`) to a current major, push it, and bump the rev Blinc pins. zyntax's local main is ahead of its origin, so this needs a branch from the pinned rev or a push of that work first.\n- Blinc: track a lockfile CI resolves from. The local-dev `[patch]` that points zyntax at a checkout rewrites the zyntax entries, so a tracked lock would churn locally unless CI keeps its own.","files":null}]}